# Findings trivy-scan.sh may ignore, one ID per line, each with its reason beside it.
#
# Same doctrine as .scan-allowlist: every line is a REVIEWABLE CLAIM that the finding does not
# apply to this package, never a way to quieten a real one. Empty is the normal state and a
# non-empty file should be explained in the pull request that adds to it.
#
# Before adding a line, try the fix: a base-image bump, or a bump of the pinned tool. An exception
# without an attempt at a fix is a decision the next maintainer inherits without the context.
#
# Format: <ID>  [# reason, and what would make this line go away]

# DS-0002 (Dockerfile has no USER). Deliberate and required by the platform: Cloudron starts the
# container as root so it can chown /app/data (a bind mount whose ownership is not ours), and
# start.sh drops to the cloudron user with gosu before exec'ing agentgateway (start.sh:95). A USER
# line here would break the chown and the app would not start. This line goes away only if Cloudron
# changes that convention.
DS-0002
